<p>Gen Z (18-29):           245 eggs / yr (+7.0% vs national) Millennials (30-44):     238 eggs / yr (+3.9%) Gen X (45-59):           224 eggs / yr (-2.2%) Boomers (60-74):         218 eggs / yr (-4.8%) Silent (75+):            208 eggs / yr (-9.2%)</p>
<p>Generational transition is on net positive for category volume.</p>
<p>protein and cholesterol narrative tailwinds:</p>
<p>Wave 11 driver-rank shifts vs Wave 7: &#x27;High in protein&#x27;:                         8th -&gt; 3rd (+5) &#x27;Heart-healthy / cholesterol-friendly&#x27;:   11th -&gt; 8th (+3) &#x27;Product of New Zealand / NZ-Made&#x27;:        5th -&gt; 2nd (+3)</p>
<p>Heart Foundation NZ current position: healthy population can include eggs in a heart-healthy diet; at-risk individuals can eat up to 6 eggs / week. Material softening vs the late-1990s Heart Foundation NZ &quot;limit to three per week&quot; framing.</p>
