<p>Calthorpe Part 5 [00:15:48]: &quot;roughly 20 to 25% of free-range buyers are price-sensitive flippers under genuine budget pressure.&quot;</p>
<p>Implication: commodity free-range premium tier carries consumer-side headwind from cost-of-living elasticity. specialty premium tier (pasture-raised, omega-3, certified organic) is much more durable - top-2-income skewed buyers with 4-9% switch rates.</p>
<h3>4. premium-tier economics and buyer skew</h3>
<p>ACII Wave 11 Egg Addendum sec. 4 (vs barn 12-pack at NZ$7.00):</p>
